hadiths[76]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7948","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa Al-Asadi told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Hafs bin Omar bin Abi told me Al-Ghataf, a client of Banu Sahm, on the authority of Abu Al-Zinad, on the authority of Al-Araj, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “O Abu Hurairah, learn The obligatory duties and teach him, for he is half of knowledge, and he will be forgotten, and he will be the first to be taken away from my nation.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7948 - Hafs bin Omar Wah Bumrah"
"7949","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abdul Rahman bin Ziyad bin told me Anam Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Rafi’ Al-Tanukhi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, may God be pleased with them, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace God, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Knowledge is of three things, and anything other than that is a virtue: a decisive sign, an established Sunnah, or a just obligation.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7949 - Both hadiths are weak"
"7950","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Al-Fadl bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Al-Nadr bin Shumail told us, he informed us Auf bin Abi Jamila, on the authority of Sulayman bin Jabir Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Learn the Qur’an and teach it to the people, and learn the religious duties and teach it to the people. Indeed, I am a person who will be arrested, and knowledge will be captured and temptations will appear.” Until the two disagree about the obligation, they will not find anyone to fulfill it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. And he has an illness on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Ishaq, on the authority of Bishr bin Musa, on the authority of Hawdha bin Khalifa, on the authority of Awf.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7950 - True"
"7951","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Hudha bin Khalifa told us, Awf told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Suleiman bin Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Learn the obligatory duties and teach them to the people, for I am a person under arrest. And knowledge will be withheld until the two disagree about the obligatory duty and find no one to separate between them.” Al-Hakim said: “And if they disagree, then the ruling is By Al-Nadhar bin Shumayl"
"7952","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuli, and Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl Al-Bajli told us, they said: Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi, Abu Hilal Al-Rasibi told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, wrote To Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari: “When you are mesmerizing, then have fun with archery, and if you talk, then talk about the obligatory prayers.” This, even if it was suspended. It has an authentic chain of narration and is supported by his saying, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Follow the example of those after me, Abu Bakr and Omar.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7952 - True"
"7953","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub narrated to us, Ibrahim bin Marzuq narrated to us, Wahb bin Jarir narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, and he narrated to us Abu Al-Abbas Al-Mahboubi, Ahmed bin Sayyar told us, Muhammad bin Kathir told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, On the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, he said: “Whoever among you has read the Qur’an, let him learn the obligatory prayers. If a Bedouin meets him, he says: Oh. Migrant, do you read the Qur’an? He says: Yes, and he says: And I read the Qur’an, and the Bedouin says: Do you assume it, O immigrant? If he said: Yes, he said: An increase in goodness, and if he said: No, I thought it was him. He said: Why did he prefer you over me, O immigrant?” The ruler said: “This is a correct position.” According to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, there is a witness to the messenger that we presented.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7953 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7954","Ahmad bin Salman, the jurist, told us: Hilal bin Al-Ala’ Al-Raqi told us, Ubayy told us, Ubayd Allah bin Amr Al-Raqi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: The wife of Saad bin Al-Rabi’ came and said: O Messenger of God, these are the two daughters of Saad bin Al-Rabi’ Their father was killed as a martyr on the day of Uhud, and their uncle took their money and did not leave any money for them, so he said: “May God decide that.” So it was revealed. The inheritance verse, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to their uncle and said: “Give Sa’d’s two daughters two-thirds, and their mother an eighth, and whatever is left is “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7954 - True"
"7955","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr bin Sabiq Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zinad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, he said: “If a man or woman dies and leaves behind one daughter She gets half, and if there are two or more, then two-thirds gets them, and if there is a male with them, then it is not obligatory for any of them. And someone begins to share with them an obligation, and he is given his share, and whatever remains after that is for the child among them. {For the male is like a portion The two females} [An-Nisa: 11] If there are two, then the females above that are entitled to two-thirds. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.” Al-Hakim said: “The statements of Zayd bin Thabit are proof for all the Companions.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7955 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7956","Abu Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Wazir Al-Tajer told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad bin Amr told us, about Abu Salamah, that Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, took Zayd bin Thabit’s ride and said to him: Step aside, O cousin of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He greeted him and said: “This is what we do to our elders and scholars.”"
"7957","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, the jurist told us Muhammad bin Ayyub, Musa bin Ismail told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Badr told us, on the authority of his father, On the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The two, and whatever is above them, is a group.”"
"7958","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Usayd bin Asim told us, Al-Hussein bin Hafs told us, Sufyan told us, On the authority of Abu Qays al-Awdi, on the authority of Huzail ibn Shurahbil, he said: I came to Abu Musa and Salman ibn Rabi’ah regarding a daughter, a son’s daughter, and a father’s sister. And a mother, so they said: Half to the daughter and half to the sister, and they said: Come to Ibn Masoud, for he will follow us. So I came to him and informed him, and he said: I have Then I have gone astray, and I am not of the rightly guided, but “I decree according to what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed: for the daughter one-half and for the son’s daughter one-sixth.” Whatever remains is for the sister. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7958 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7959","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, he said: “The inheritance of brothers from the father and mother is that they do not inherit with the male child nor “With the son being begotten, nor with the father.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and they agreed on no other hadith like this. The fatwa of Zaid bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him:
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7959 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7960","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Abdullah bin Ruh Al-Madaini told us, Shababah bin Suwar told us, Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them, that he entered upon Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, and said: “Indeed “The two brothers do not substitute the mother for a third.” God Almighty said: “And if he has brothers, then to his mother is one-sixth” [An-Nisa’: 11] “So the brothers are with the tongue of Your people are not brothers.” Then Othman bin Affan said: “I cannot undo what happened before me and passed through the ages, and people inherited it.” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7960 - True"
"7961","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Abdul Rahman bin Abi Al-Zanad told me, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, that he used to say: “Brothers in Arab speech are brothers and upwards.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7961 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7962","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz and Abu Yahya Ahmad bin Muhammad Al-Samarqandi told us, saying: Abu Abdullah Muhammad told us Bin Nasr Al-Imam, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Khallad Al-Bahili told us, Abdul-Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed told us, Khaled Al-Hadha told us, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The most noble of my nation is Zayd bin Thabit.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7962 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7963","Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, said: “Umar, may God be pleased with him, came with a woman and two fathers: so he made for the woman A quarter, and the mother gets a third of what remains, and the father gets what remains. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7963 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7964","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh told me, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to me, Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father Saeed bin Masruq, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: “God would not Come to see me preferring a mother to a grandfather.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7964 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7965","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ali Al-San’ani informed us of Mecca, which God Almighty protected. Ibrahim bin Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us. Abd al-Razzaq, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Ibn Tawus informed me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar ibn al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him He made a will at the time of death, and said: “What did you say about calamity?” Ibn Abbas said: What did you say? He said: “He who has no children.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. It is in the original a chain of transmission, as it is in his sermon, and I did not review it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding something I did not review with him.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7965 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7966","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih told us, Ahmad bin Najda told us, Yahya bin Abdul Hamid told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, that a man said: O Messenger of God, what The fatigue? He said: “Have you not heard the verse that was revealed in the summer: ‘They ask you for a fatwa. Say, ‘Allah gives you a fatwa regarding the caliphate.’” [An-Nisa: 176] And the caliphate is he who leaves no child. Nor a father. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7966 - Al-Hamani is weak"
"7967","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khorasani, Al-Adl in Baghdad, told us, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Dawud Al-Hafari told us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, settled the debt before... “The will” as you read it “after a bequeathed bequest or a debt” [An-Nisa: 12] and that the notables of the mother’s sons inherit inheritance to the exclusion of their sons. Causes, brothers from the mother, brothers from the father, and the mother are closer than brothers from the father “This is a hadith that people narrated on the authority of my father Ishaq, and Al-Harith bin Abdullah on the road, so the two sheikhs did not narrate it, and this fatwa was authenticated on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7967 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7968","Just as Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me, about His father, on the authority of Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, he said: “The inheritance of brothers from the father if there is no one of the mother’s sons with them.” And the father is like the inheritance of the brothers from the father and mother, whether their males are like their males and their females are like their females, and if the brothers come together from The father, the mother, and the brothers on the father’s side, and among the sons of the father and the mother there was a male, so there is no inheritance with him for any of the brothers on the father’s side.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7968 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7969","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abu Umayyah bin Ya’la Al-Thaqafi told us, On the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of Amr ibn Wahb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, in al-Musharrataka, he said: “They claimed that their father was some kind of donkey.” “The father increased them except by closeness and shared among them the third.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. He did not narrate it and explain it with the hadith that “”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7969 - True"
"7970","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Imran bin Abi Laila told us, my father informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Shabi, on the authority of Omar, Ali, Abdullah, and Zaid, may God be pleased with them, in a mother, a husband, and paternal brothers, a mother, and brothers. For a mother: “The brothers from the father and mother are partners with the brothers from the mother in a third of them. This is because they said they are all the sons of a mother.” And the father only increased their closeness, for they are partners in the third.”"
"7971","Abu Yahya Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Samarqandi told us, Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Nasr al-Imam told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, And Mahmoud bin Adam, they said: Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, Musab bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: “Something that you do not find in the Book of God Almighty nor in the judgment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but you find it among all people for the daughter.” “Half and half to the sister.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7971 - True"
"7972","Abu Yahya al-Samarqandi told us, Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Yazid, that he said: Ibn Al-Zubayr used to say regarding a daughter and a sister: The money is for the daughter, so I said: “Indeed, Mu’adh decreed Among us in Yemen, half goes to the daughter and half to the sister.” He said: “You are my messenger to Al-Walid ibn Utbah - who was his judge in Kufa - so give him orders.” So let him take that as “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7972 - True"
"7973","Abu Amr Othman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq told us, in Baghdad, Ahmed bin Malaab bin Hayyan told us, Ali bin Asim told us, Abdullah told us Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to me: “Add money to the duties, and what It remains for the first man mentioned.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, for Ali bin Asim is truthful, and they did not narrate it. Sufyan al-Thawri sent it. Sufyan bin Uyaynah, Ibn Jurayj, and Muammar bin Rashid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus,"
"7974","As for the hadith of Al-Thawri, Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Sufyan told us ""The revolutionary"""
"7975","As for the hadith of Ibn Uyaynah, Abu Yahya al-Samarqandi told us, Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Sufyan told us Ibn Uyaynah"
"7976","As for the hadith of Ibn Jurayj, Abu Yahya informed us, Muhammad ibn Nasr told us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj."
"7977","As for the hadith of Muammar,
So we informed Abu Abbas al-Sayyari, Abu al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah informed, Muammar informed, all of them, about Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Append the money With the obligatory duties, whatever the obligatory duties remain, it belongs to the closest male man.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7973 - Rather, they unanimously agreed that it was weak, meaning Ali bin Asim."
"7978","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaydi told us, Sufyan told us, and Sufyan told us. Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub informed, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulaiman informed, Al-Shafi’i informed, Sufyan informed, and Abu Bakr bin Ishaq informed us, Abu Muslim reported, Al-Qanabi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaysah ibn Dhu’ayb, who said: The grandmother came to Abu Bakr. May God be pleased with him after the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: I have a right. The son of a son or the son of a daughter of mine died. He said: I did not know of you in The Book of God is true, and I have not heard anything from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about it. I will ask the people, so he asked them. Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah Radi testified. God said, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave her a sixth.” He said: Who heard that with you? Muhammad bin Maslamah testified, so Abu Bakr gave her a sixth: “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7978 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7979","Abu Yahya Al-Samarqandi told us, Muhammad bin Nasr Al-Imam told us, Ishaq told us, Abd al-Razzaq told us, Muammar told us, about Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, said: A man came to Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, and said: A man died and left his daughter and sister to his father. And his mother, so he said: “His daughter gets half, but his sister gets nothing.” The man said: Omar, may God be pleased with him, ruled otherwise, and gave the daughter half. Regarding the half sister, Ibn Abbas said: “Do you know better, or God?” I did not know what this was about until I met Ibn Tawus, and I mentioned the hadith of Al-Zuhri to him, and he said: My father told me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: God Almighty said: {If a man dies having no child and having a sister, then she gets half of what he left behind} [An-Nisa: 176]. Ibn Abbas said: “Then you said, ‘You are for her. Half, even if he has a son.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7979 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7980","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abu Muammar told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Ubaid, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, he said: Omar said: Who has the authority on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said: I have. He said: What do you have? I said: “He gave him a sixth.” He said: “With whom?” I said: I don’t know. He said: “I don’t know.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7980 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7981","Abu Abdullah told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan told us, Abu Muammar told us, Wahib told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. God said on their behalf, “Abu Bakr, may God be pleased with him, made him a father,” meaning the grandfather, “this is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7981 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7982","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Kharijah bin Zayd bin Thabit, on the authority of his father, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, when he consulted them about the inheritance of the grandfather and brothers, he said Zaid: “My opinion was that the brothers had more right to inheritance than the grandfather, and Omar, may God be pleased with him, believed at that time that the grandfather had more right to inheritance. His father’s son from his brothers.” Zaid said: “So I debated with Omar and gave an example to Omar about that, and he gave Ali bin Abi Talib and Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with them, told Umar, for example, that day they would hit the torrent and drain it in the manner of Zayd. This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7982 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7983","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ismail bin Abi Uwais told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim told us Bin Uqba, on the authority of his uncle Musa bin Uqba, who said: Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told us that Marwan bin Al-Hakam told him that Omar, may God be pleased with him, when He was stabbed and said: “Indeed, I saw in seriousness an opinion, so if you decide that you should follow it.” Uthman said: “If we follow your opinion, then it is guidance. The Sheikh before you, and what a good opinion he was.” This hadith is authentic according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7983 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7984","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, Abu Kamil Al-Jahdari told us, Al-Fadl bin Suleiman told us, Musa bin Uqba narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yahya bin Al-Walid bin Ubadah, on the authority of Ubadah bin Al-Samit, may God be pleased with him, who said: “Indeed, who The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed for the two grandmothers one-sixth of the inheritance between them equally. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. """"
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7984 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7985","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Ismail bin Ishaq al-Qadi told us, Ali bin Abdullah al-Madani told us, Ya’qub told us Bin Ibrahim bin Saad, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim bin Abdullah bin Shihab told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that he said: “The first to perform the obligatory duties was Omar, may God be pleased with him. “God has put forward and delayed. Whoever God has delayed, no obligatory prayer has been committed.” So it was said to him: Which of them has God put forward and which has He delayed? He said: “Every obligation that God Almighty and Majestic has not removed from one obligation except to another obligation, this is what God Almighty and Majestic has provided, and every obligation if She missed her obligation, she only had what remained, and that is the one whom God Almighty has delayed, like the husband, the wife, and the mother, and the one who has delayed Like sisters and daughters, when those who brought God Almighty forward and those who came back are gathered, they will begin with those who came first, and he will be given his full right. If anything remains, it is “For whoever delays it, and if nothing remains, then nothing remains for him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7985 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7986","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Abu Utbah Ahmad bin Al-Faraj told us, Baqiyya bin Al-Walid told us, Abu Salamah Al-Homsi told me Suleiman bin Sulaym, on the authority of Omar bin Ruba, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Basri, on the authority of Wathilah bin Al-Asqa’, may God be pleased with him On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A woman possesses three inheritances: her freed man, her foundling, and the child over whom she cursed.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not take it out.”"
"7987","Abu Abdullah Ishaq bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz and Abu Yahya Al-Samarqandi informed us, saying: Muhammad bin Nasr Al-Imam told us, told us: Yahya bin Yahya reported from Abbad bin Al-Awwam, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him. He said regarding the inheritance of Ibn al-Mala’ana: “His entire inheritance is for his mother.” This is a hadith whose narrators are all trustworthy, and it is a messenger and has a witness.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7987 - Sent"
"7988","Abu Yahya alone informed us: Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Abd al-A’la bin Hammad told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of a man from the Levant, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said regarding the son of Al-Mala’ana: “His mother bound him.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7988 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7989","Abu Yahya told us, Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Yahya bin Abi Bukayr told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman, On the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: “A dispute was made to Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, regarding the son of He who was cursed, so he gave his inheritance to his mother and made her his concubine.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it, and this is Muhammad bin Ishaq. Al-Saghani, without a doubt.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7989 - True"
"7990","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, going back to the beginning, Al-Rabi’ bin Suleiman told us, Al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Abu Yusuf, On the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Loyalty is a flesh like the flesh of lineage that cannot be sold.” It shall not be given as a gift.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it."
"7991","Abdul Rahman bin Hamdan told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Mahran told us, Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Ismail Ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Loyalty is a piece of lineage that cannot be sold or sold.” be given away
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7991 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7992","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told us, saying: Muhammad bin Ayyub told us, Amr bin Husayn informed us. Al-Uqaili, Muammar bin Sulaiman told us, Salem bin Abi Al-Dhayal told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no striving in Islam. Whoever strives during pre-Islamic times has joined him to his clan, and whoever claims a son from someone other than He did not inherit and was not bequeathed.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it or witness it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7992 - Perhaps it is a topic"
"7993","What Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Sulami told us, Muhammad bin Bakkar bin Bilal told us, Muhammad bin Rashid told us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever claims a son from a nation He owns it or from a free woman with whom he has committed prostitution, then he shall not join it nor inherit, and he was born of adultery to whoever his mother’s family were.”"
"7994","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq and Ali bin Hamshadh told us, saying: Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The notables of the mother’s sons inherit from each other, not the descendants of the clans.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7994 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7995","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Musa bin Al-Hasan bin Abbad told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The wife of Saad bin Al-Rabi’ came, She said: O Messenger of God, these are the daughters of Saad bin Al-Rabi’. Their father was killed with you as a martyr on the day of Uhud, and their uncle took their money and did not leave. They had money, and he said: “God will decide about that.” He said: Then the verse about inheritance was revealed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to their uncle and said: “Give “Saad’s two daughters, two-thirds, and their mother, one-eighth, and whatever remains is yours.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it."
"7996","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Ishaq bin Ayyub Al-Imam told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Zakaria bin Yahya told us, Abdullah bin Jafar, Abdullah bin Dinar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approached a donkey and found it. A man, and he said: O Messenger of God, a man left behind his paternal aunt and his maternal aunt, and he has no heir other than them. He said: Then he raised his head to the sky, and said: “Oh God, a man. He left behind his paternal aunt and maternal uncle and has no heir other than them.” Then he said: “Where is the questioner?” He said: Here I am. He said: “They have no inheritance.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. Abdullah bin Ja’far al-Madani, even if he witnessed it, His son Ali has a bad memory, so he is not one of those whose hadiths are neglected and he has a witness: “"
"7997","As Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Harun Al-Awdi told us, Sulayman bin Dawud Al-Shazakuni told us, Ismail bin Ibrahim, Muhammad bin Amr bin Alqamah told us, on the authority of Sharik bin Abi Nimr, that Al-Harith bin Abdullah told him that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the inheritance of a paternal aunt and paternal aunt. He remained silent, then Gabriel, peace be upon him, came down to him and said: “Gabriel told me that no ""an inheritance for them"""
"7998","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz told us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Musa bin Ishaq Al-Tamimi told us, Abu Nu’aym Dirar bin Surad told us, On the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, rode to Quba’, with saddlebags on the donkey, and said: “I ask God Almighty for guidance regarding the inheritance of a paternal aunt and maternal aunt.” So God Almighty revealed to him That they have no inheritance. “The hadith of Abdullah bin Jaafar has been authenticated with this evidence, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7999","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hassan bin Ayyub told us, Ali bin Abdul-Aziz told us, Abu Ubaid told us, Saeed bin Ufayr told me, Alwan told me Ibn Dawud, on the authority of Salih Ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Humaid Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Awf, on the authority of his father, he said: I entered upon Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of him, during his illness in which he died, I went back to him and heard him say: “I wish I had asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about the inheritance of a paternal aunt and maternal aunt. I have a need for it.”"
"8000","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Ibn Abi Al-Zanad told me, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, he said: “The paternal aunt, the paternal sister of the father and the mother, nor the paternal aunt, nor whoever is further away shall not inherit. Lineage from the deceased. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8000 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8001","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Al-Hasan bin Affan told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Al-Hasan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: “No way, no way, where is Ibn Masoud? The immigrants used to inherit inheritance, not the Bedouins.” So it was revealed. {And those of kinship are closer to one another} [Al-Ahzab: 6] “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8001 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8002","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, the martyr sheikh of the Imam, the son of the Imam, Abu Zakaria Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya Al-Dhuhli, Musaddad narrated to us, Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Badil bin Maysara, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Amer Al-Hawzani, on the authority of Al-Muqadam Al-Kindi, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I am the master of one who has no master.” To him I inherit his wealth and I pay off his debts, and the maternal uncle is the heir of someone who has no heirs, he inherits his wealth and I pay off his debts.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8002 - Ali bin Abi Talha Ahmad said reprehensible things to him, but Al-Bukhari did not narrate to him"
"8003","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan Al-Amiri told us, Yahya bin Adam told us, Israel told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Hani, and on the authority of Hubayra ibn Yarim, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Leave the female slave with “Her aunt, for the aunt is a mother.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8003 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8004","Abu Abdullah Al-Shaybani and Abu Yahya Al-Samarqandi told us, saying: Muhammad bin Nasr Al-Imam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Mukhlid bin Zayd Al-Jazari reported, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Allah and His Messenger are the masters of those who have no masters, and the maternal uncle is the heir of those who have no heirs.” This is an authentic hadith based on The condition of the two sheikhs and they did not include it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8004 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8005","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir Al-Hazami told us, Muhammad bin Sadaqat al-Fadaki, Ibn Abi al-Zinad told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may God be pleased with him, said: Among us This verse was revealed: {And those of kinship are closer to one another in the Book of God} [Al-Ahzab: 6] He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace There was a brotherhood between a man from among the Muhajireen and a man from among the Ansar, and we did not doubt that we would inherit something if Kaab were to die and had no one to inherit it. So I thought that I inherit from him, and if I were to perish, he would inherit from me” until this verse was revealed: “And the relatives of relatives are closer to one another” [Al-Ahzab: 6] “This is a hadith. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8005 - True"
"8006","Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Hafiz told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Abi Hakim, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Yahya ibn Ya`mar, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, may God be pleased with him, that he was given the inheritance of a Jew and his A Muslim heir, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Islam increases and does not decrease.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration and it was not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8006 - True"
"8007","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muhammad bin Amr told me, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A Muslim does not inherit “The Christian, unless it is his male or female slave.” Muhammad ibn Amr. This is Al-Yafi’i from the people of Egypt. The hadith is authentic and authentic. The original is the hadith of Amr bin Shuaib, who said:
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8007 - True"
"8008","Abu Al-Abbas told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Al-Khalil bin Murrah told me, about Qatada, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A Muslim does not inherit from an infidel, nor does an infidel inherit from a Muslim.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8008 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8009","Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Yaqoub and Abu Yahya Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Samarqandi informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Imam told us, they told us: Yahya bin Yahya, Abd al-Aziz bin Muhammad reported, on the authority of Ja`far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, “Umm Kulthum is the daughter of Ali, may God be pleased with her.” About them, she and her son Zaid bin Omar bin Al-Khattab died on the same day, and it is not known which of the two of them died before, so she did not inherit from him and he did not inherit from her, although The people of Siffin did not inherit from one another, and the people of Al-Harrah did not inherit from each other.” This hadith, its chain of transmission is authentic, and it contains benefits, including that Umm Kulthum She bore Omar a son, but as for the other benefit, he has a witness.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8009 - True"
"8010","Abu Abdullah and Abu Yahya told us, saying: Muhammad bin Nasr told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Kharijah bin Musab told us, On the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that “a deceased would not inherit from the deceased if he did not It is known which of them died before its owner.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8010 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8011","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Qasim bin Al-Qasim Al-Sayyari told us about Marwa, Muhammad bin Musa bin Hatim told us, Ali bin Al-Hassan bin Shaqiq told us, he informed us Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Yazid, the grammarian, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them: {And those whose oaths are tied, go to them. Their share} [An-Nisa: 33] He said: “A man used to ally himself with another man while there was no blood relationship between them, so that one of them would inherit from the other.” So God abolished that with the Anfal: {And the first The relatives are more worthy of one another in the Book of God} [Al-Ahzab: 6]
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8011 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8012","Abu Yahya Al-Samarqandi told us, Muhammad bin Nasr Al-Imam told us, Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, about His father, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Abu Hassan told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, that he heard Muadh ibn Jabal, may God be pleased with him, say while he was on Al-Minbar: “The wealth of a man who left behind his daughter and sister was inherited, and half was given to his daughter and half to his sister. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is still alive.” “Show them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8012 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8013","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmed Al-Khayyat told me about Burdan Bridge, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, Amr ibn Dinar told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, that a man died, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “They sought an heir for him,” but there was only one of his heirs who freed him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Give it to him.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, and they did not narrate it “except that Hammad bin Salamah and Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated it, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Awsaja, the client of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas.”"
"8014","As for the hadith of Hammad, “Abu Abdullah al-Saffar told us, Muhammad bin Salamah told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Hammad bin Salamah informed us.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8013 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8015","As for the hadith of Ibn Uyaynah
So Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: He told me Awsaja, the client of Ibn Abbas, said: I heard Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, saying: “A man died during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He left no heirs or relatives except a slave whom he freed and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave him the inheritance.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8015 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8016","Ahmad bin Ja’far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Tahman, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: They disputed with Ali, may God be pleased with him, regarding He was born cursed, and his father’s family came asking for his inheritance. He said, “Indeed, his father had disowned him.” So he gave his mother the inheritance and made her A group and did not give them anything “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, even if it is based on the ruling of the Commander of the Faithful, then it is strange from his fatwas.” And its rulings”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8016 - Sahih Gharib"
"8017","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Abdullah bin Ata told us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, said: A woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: I gave alms to my mother in charity. Then she died and the charity was returned to me, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Your reward is due and your charity is returned to you.” Narrated by Sufyan Al-Thawri, And others, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father"
"8018","Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Ibn Abi Laila told us, and Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ata, On the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, he said: A woman came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My mother died and she must fast. For two months, he said: “Fast on her behalf.” She said: She has a Hajj due, so he said: “Perform the Hajj on her behalf.” She said: “I have given in charity to a slave girl.” He said: “I have May God reward you and restore your inheritance. This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration. They did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8018 - True"
"8019","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Hilal, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd bin Abdul Rabbo, He is the one who was shown the call because “he gave alms to his parents, then they died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned it to him as an inheritance.” This is an authentic hadith according to The condition of the two sheikhs is that Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm heard it from Abdullah bin Zayd and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8019 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"8020","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Bishr bin Musa told us, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Muhammad, and Abdullah, my son Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hazm, that Abdullah bin Zayd bin Abdul Rabbo came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O Messenger of God, this wall of mine is a charity and it belongs to God and His Messenger. Then his parents came and said: O Messenger of God, it was the basis for our livelihood. “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned it to them, then they died and their son inherited it after them.” This is an authentic hadith according to the two sheikhs’ conditions as well. The most correct of what was narrated in the paths of this hadith is:
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 8020 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"8021","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani did not tell us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed, Ubaid Allah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of his grandfather Abdullah bin Zaid, that he gave alms With a wall for him, his parents came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, it was the value of our faces and we had nothing else. So he called Abdullah and said: “Indeed, God Almighty has accepted your charity and returned it to your parents.” Bashir said: “So we inherited it after that” and this The hadith, even if its chain of transmission is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, then I do not see that Bashir bin Muhammad Al-Ansari heard from his grandfather Abdullah bin Zaid. The two sheikhs left out the hadith of Abdullah bin Zaid regarding the call to prayer and the vision that he related to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in this regard. The chain of transmission precedes the death of Abdullah bin Zaid. It was said that he was martyred by Uhud, and it was said that it occurred shortly after that, and God knows best."
"8022",""
"8023","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Abdul Rahman Ahmad bin Shuaib Al-Nasa’i narrated in Egypt, and Abdullah bin Zaydan Al-Bajli narrated in Kufa, They said: Abdullah bin Al-Kindi told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If a boy initiates the initiation, he inherits and pray for him.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it, and I may find it From the hadith of Al-Thawri, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, he was detained, so I used to judge by him “the last book of religious duties.”
["
